</ul></div></div><h2 class="sectionedit1" id="tan">Tan</h2><div class="level2"></div><h3 class="sectionedit2" id="format">Format</h3><div class="level3"><p><strong>tan</strong> ( <em>expression</em> )</p></div><h3 class="sectionedit3" id="description">Description</h3><div class="level3"><p>Computes the tangent of <em>expression</em>. <em>Expression</em> must be in radians.</p></div><h3 class="sectionedit4" id="note">Note</h3><div class="level3"><p>The tan function does not produce an exact result.</p></div><h3 class="sectionedit5" id="see_also">See Also</h3><div class="level3"><p><a href="el_acos.html" class="wikilink1" title="el:acos">Acos</a>, <a href="el_asin.html" class="wikilink1" title="el:asin">Asin</a>, <a href="el_atan.html" class="wikilink1" title="el:atan">Atan</a>, <a href="el_sin.html" class="wikilink1" title="el:sin">Sin</a>, <a href="el_cos.html" class="wikilink1" title="el:cos">Cos</a>, <a href="el_degrees.html" class="wikilink1" title="el:degrees">Degrees</a>, <a href="el_radians.html" class="wikilink1" title="el:radians">Radians</a></p></div><h3 class="sectionedit6" id="example">Example</h3><div class="level3"><pre class="code">clgcolor black# draw a line across the graphic outputline 0,150,300,150# where do we startlastx = 0lasty = tan(0) * 50 + 150# now step across the line and drawfor x = 0 to 300 step 5   angle = x / 300 * 2 * pi   y = tan(angle) * 50 + 150   line lastx, lasty, x, y   lastx = x   lasty = ynext x</pre><p>Draws<a href="http://doc.basic256.org/lib/exe/detail.php?id=el_tan&amp;media=el:tan.jpg" class="media wikilink2" title="el:tan.jpg"><img src="http://doc.basic256.org/lib/exe/el:tan.jpg" class="media" title="tan.jpg" alt="tan.jpg" /></a></p></div>                                    </div>                <div class="docInfo"><bdi>el/tan.txt</bdi> · Last modified: 2014/01/11 23:26 (external edit)</div>                            </div></div>            <hr class="a11y" />     